heading: "Google Ads budget calculator"
standfirst: "Work backwards from the leads or sales you want each month to the monthly and daily budget it takes, using your own cost per click and conversion rate."
title: "Google Ads Budget Calculator: Monthly and Daily | DigitalFadi"
description: "Free Google Ads budget calculator. Enter the leads or sales you want, your cost per click and conversion rate, and get the monthly and daily budget you need."
faqs:
  - q: "How do I calculate my Google Ads budget?"
    a: "Divide the number of conversions you want by your conversion rate to get the clicks you need, then multiply by your average cost per click. For 30 leads a month at a 5 percent conversion rate and a 3 dollar cost per click, you need 600 clicks, which is a budget of 1,800 a month."
  - q: "How do I turn a monthly budget into a daily budget?"
    a: "Divide the monthly budget by 30.4, the average number of days in a month. Google Ads uses the same figure: over a month it will not charge more than your average daily budget multiplied by 30.4, although spend can be higher on individual days."
  - q: "Where do I find my cost per click and conversion rate?"
    a: "If the account has been running, use the last 90 days from the Campaigns view, ideally for the campaigns you plan to fund. For a new account, Keyword Planner gives estimated cost per click ranges for your keywords, and your website's conversion rate from other traffic is a starting point for the conversion rate."
  - q: "Why do I need more budget than the calculator says?"
    a: "The result assumes your cost per click and conversion rate stay the same as you spend more. In practice, extra budget often buys less relevant clicks at higher prices, so results per dollar usually fall a little as spend grows. Use the range table to see what happens if your numbers are worse than expected."
  - q: "Is the information I enter saved?"
    a: "Yes, in this browser only, so your figures are still there next time on the same device. Nothing is uploaded or sent anywhere, including to me. The Clear button removes them."
---
